   "title": "README — H3 LongTake character swap",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 LongTake — Character swap (Ref2VA)\n\nThe dancer/performer of the source video is replaced by the character of `<Picture 1>`, keeping the room, motion and camera of `<Video 1>`.\n\n- Picture: the character **framed like the video** (full body if the video is full body) and, ideally, on a plain background; if the picture has its own scenery, say in the prompt \"do not use the wall/lights from <Picture 1>\" or connect a rembg mask to `ref_mask_1` (the node flattens the background).\n- Prompt (in the PROMPT node): \"<Video 1> provides the full performance, motion, timing, camera distance and framing. Replace the dancer with the character from <Picture 1>: <describe hair, face, outfit>. Keep the room, lighting and background exactly as in <Video 1>.\"\n- Measured (10 s): identity similarity 0.74–0.86 to the picture with plain Ref2VA; motion lag −1…−3 frames.\n\nSteps: `dry_run=true` → `max_clips=2` → `max_clips=0` → Ctrl+M on the Stitch. One clip in memory whatever the length."
   ],
